# The outline parser is line-anchored, and Git's core.autocrlf=true rewrites every text
# file with CRLF on checkout. That made `npm run generate` REFUSE TO WRITE on a fresh
# Windows clone - the deck could not be rebuilt from its own source. Normalise to LF in
# the working tree, not just in the repository, so every machine builds the same deck.
#
# parse-outline.mjs also strips CR defensively, so a machine that ignores this file still
# works. Both, because the failure is silent-looking: it reads as missing slide content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fonts, images and the exported deck are binary. Never touch their bytes.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.pptx  binary

# Key-per-file demo secrets: the FILE CONTENTS are the configuration value, so a stray
# newline would change what the demo reads back. Leave them exactly as written.
demos/d23-key-per-file/secrets/** -text
